## Notes

- **bd71d0715** is the single largest commit by a wide margin: a full-stack feature introducing the agentic insights extraction pipeline (71 files, 8,021 insertions). It includes a new Prisma schema, worker, multiple AI agent steps, evaluation harness scaffolding, and a complete React UI flow. Estimated at 40 hours reflecting weeks of iterative development squashed into one PR.
- **1fb7091cd** (Try Agentic Insights) represents a major architectural pivot from a multi-step workflow to a single agent with tool calls, accompanied by new evaluation data and source-reference deduplication.
- **33c972110** introduces a bespoke evaluation framework (eval package, scorers, vitest config) requiring substantial design work.
- **f05990347** replaces a tree-based dependency algorithm with a proper directed acyclic graph implementation, deleting ~1,400 lines and re-testing thoroughly.
- **b184fcfa2** and **6db6101fd** are large primarily due to deletion of dead code, legacy seed files, and dropped database tables — high file counts but lower design complexity than insertion-heavy PRs.
- Several commits on 2025-12-05 (maximize build space, remove stuff, use rmz, expose logger) are CI/DevOps housekeeping tasks with negligible complexity and under 30 minutes of effort each.
